Input: {"question": "When is the feast day of Saint Marcellus?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d00", "start": 0, "end": 143, "text": "Marcellus of Capua Marcellus of Capua was a third- or fourth-century martyr who was inserted in the General Roman Calendar in the 13th century."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d00", "start": 144, "end": 228, "text": "He is recognized as a saint by the Catholic Church, with 7 October as his feast day."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d00", "start": 229, "end": 508, "text": "Untrustworthy legends associated him with a Saint Apuleius, which led to them being mentioned together in some editions of the Roman Martyrology, but the name of Apuleius has been removed from that official list of saints of the Catholic Church, as without historical foundation."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d00", "start": 509, "end": 603, "text": "In the Tridentine Calendar, Marcellus was commemorated with Apuleius and two other saints on 7"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d01", "start": 0, "end": 201, "text": "CatholicSaints.Info » Blog Archive » Saint Marcellus of Capua CatholicSaints.Info notes about your extended family in heaven Saint Marcellus of Capua Memorial 7 October Profile Student of Simon Magus ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d01", "start": 202, "end": 363, "text": "Converted to Christianity by Saint Peter the Apostle ; an old tradition says that he was one of the people who interred the body of Saint Peter on Vatican Hill ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d01", "start": 364, "end": 372, "text": "Martyr ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d01", "start": 373, "end": 592, "text": "Died in Capua , Italy buried outside the