uary"}, "D4S8": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d03", "start": 286, "end": 295, "text": "Marcellus"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d04", "start": 0, "end": 41, "text": "On 7 October, the feast day of Pope Mark."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d04", "start": 42, "end": 102, "text": "The Sacramentarium of Pope Gelasius assigned a mass to them."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d04", "start": 103, "end": 240, "text": "[4] In 1716, this day became the feast of Our Lady of the Rosary, and the commemoration of Marcellus and Apuleius was moved to 8 October."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d04", "start": 241, "end": 413, "text": "In 1969, Marcellus was reassigned to 15 December, while Apuleius was expunged from the official list of saints of the Catholic Church, [5] as without historical foundation."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d04", "start": 414, "end": 490, "text": "[3] Although the veneration of the two saints is very old, their existing..."}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d05", "start": 0, "end": 87, "text": "Marcellus of Tangier Saint Marcellus of Tangier or Saint Marcellus the Centurion () (c."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d05", "start": 88, "end": 200, "text": "mid 3rd century – 298 AD) is venerated as a Martyr Saint by the Catholic Church and the Eastern Orthodox Church."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d05", "start": 201, "end": 243, "text": "His feast day is celebrated on October 30."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d05", "start": 244, "end": 473, "text": "Marcellus was said to have been a centurion stationed at Tingis (modern-day Tangiers) who refused to participate in the general birthday celebrations of the Emperor Maximian, which would have entailed sacrifice to the Roman gods."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d05", "start": 474, "end": 557, "text": "Throwing off his military belt, weapons, and vine staff (the insignia of his rank)."}, "D6S6": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d05", "start": 558, "end": 605, "text": "Marcellus was soon brought before a judge named"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d06", "start": 0, "end": 74, "text": "apostate who had denied the Faith even before the outbreak of persecution."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d06", "start": 75, "end": 140, "text": "The tyrannical Maxentius had the pope seized and sent into exile."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d06", "start": 141, "end": 377, "text": "This took place at the end of 308 or the beginning of 309 according to the passages cited above from the \"Catalogus Liberianus\", which gives the length of the pontificate as no more than one year, six (or seven) months, and twenty days."}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d06", "start": 378, "end": 450, "text": "Marcellus died shortly after leaving Rome, and was venerated as a saint."}, "D7S5": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d06", "start": 451, "end": 581, "text": "His feast day was 16 January, according to the \"Depositio episcoporum\" of the Chronography of 354 and every other Roman authority."}, "D7S6": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d06", "start": 582, "end": 595, "text": "Nevertheless,"}, "D8S1": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d07", "start": 0, "end": 43, "text": "`` https : //en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php ?"}, "D8S2": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d07", "start": 44, "end": 752, "text": "title=Pope_Marcellin